    "rating": 4.4,
    "reference": "ChIJSbU-js43yUwRhiWSuMtxgHE",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Lucas Sumner",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114669413697163778920/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXxi1rweYKawnQhou8YSa83DJgHM1N0f7NXCm-FHWXS5HK3cmnkfw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Unfortunately this is yet another vet that has succumb to corporate greed. Since the change in management they have been nothing but money chasers.\n\nWhen I asked to renew my cats standard medication this month they said they would NOT GIVE HIM his medication that he needs to take everyday to LIVE because he needed his “annual exam” . Keep in mind I had been to the vet 4 TIMES with my cat in the last 7 months. They stressed that those last 4 times they never did a physical exam on my cat (despite me providing receipts that I was charged for it). Receptionist had no compassion for my situation and even after the pharmacist got involved to apologize on her behalf and gave me the pills, she felt the need to voice her frustration and tell us off again.\n\nThis unoptional “annual exam” was not informed to me the previous time I picked up his pills to give me any time to plan for it. With the 3 + weeks it can take to plan a visit at this place I had no where to go.",
        "time": 1761951159,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Mariette Gallan",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/108405697502521561799/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUpIUKhbqG1ZQWLqjGHO6B7f7iwXjS-9muqrSBN_TFFGwsZgk1SnQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "I really like this vet. Everyone is so friendly. They take the time to explain/answer any questions that I have. They took good care of Storm, my kitten.",
        "time": 1712877333,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Anthony Giroux",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102915766292407234052/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIKy1Vjas3vKhKgdGuU3mMyUhidXCZTv89ofeldmVseIavsqg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "5 years ago",
        "text": "We kept having to bring my dog back to the clinic because his eye was constantly getting infected. All they would do is prescribe some drops and then we would leave. After the fourth time, we went to a veterinarian hospital and they told us our dog needed surgery as soon as possible because he could go blind in one eye.\n\nThe surgery cost my family 3000$. They told us if the vets had properly prescribed his problem early on, his eye could have healed relatively quickly. Instead, he had to wear a cone for over a month and we had to administer 7 different types of eye drops several times a day.\n\nThankfully, he has fully recovered.",
        "time": 1602632586,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Tally Curiel",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100318365249537900665/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKogAQRxQLbU_riRayOhZo3kPpT0Pt1oOiirR3YsmGyAq_W5A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "These people are money grabbers who don’t care about your animals life. They just want money. My dog had to have an operation at the beginning of the year for her teeth, when I went in for it, I asked the vet if it would be possible while my 15 years old dog is asleep to also quickly cut and stitch (a procedure that took another vet about 10 minutes with my dog awake) a tumour that was on her foot. The vet assured me it would be done. It was not done and they expected me to pay AGAIN for another surgery to get it removed. This was absolutely gross behaviour. I do not recommend this vet. I’ll also mention the fact that we (my father and I) tried to go to the clinic to talk to the person in charge about our mistreatment and the lady acted like we were lying and was giving a pretty hostile attitude. She claimed that we did not bring her earlier (which one, we did right after the operation, twice, and two, that shouldn’t even matter because the whole point was that the vet didn’t do what she said she would do in the first place.) and that it was our fault because of that. When we mentioned we did, she said that there was no mention of it in the vets notes, which of course means we’re lying right? Because vets are all so honest right? Shame on you.",
        "time": 1728062933,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Jason Nemo",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109167588129974474080/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIkpygVg8B-kfeBB-TBQQwDU0-pM1PB-MaaHiuJSmKh3PXF0Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "I used to really like this place, but in recent years I felt like I was getting more pressure to have tests done that didn't seem necessary. Now I find out that they've been bought by Vet Strategy, a huge corporation that's been using shady business practices across the country. Suddenly all the unnecessary tests make sense.",
        "time": 1737649494,
        "translated": false
      }
